00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.760
about things like how
do we choose applicants?

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:45.315
How many people apply?

00:21:45.315 --> 00:21:48.003
Are we flexible on the age requirements?

00:21:50.037 --> 00:21:53.842
- So yeah, so when you're joining
the LAB Jumpstart program,

00:21:53.842 --> 00:21:56.420
you cannot just join the spring session,

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:58.651
you have to join for the
entirety of the session.

00:21:58.651 --> 00:22:00.843
So one of the questions that
we asked in the interviews

00:22:00.843 --> 00:22:03.306
whether or not you can
commit to the entire time.

00:22:03.306 --> 00:22:06.420
So it's not a program that split into two,

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:08.194
it's a program with two parts,

00:22:08.194 --> 00:22:10.110
if that makes sense.

00:22:10.110 --> 00:22:13.060
So you're unable to join if
you can only join for one part.

00:22:14.736 --> 00:22:18.124
Yes, so there are no
exceptions with the age.

00:22:18.124 --> 00:22:21.960
So you have to be 16 by March
2nd, that's not an us rule.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:25.243
That's a legal Rockefeller
University rule.

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:29.110
There is the separate application
for the summer program.

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:31.090
So for students who just wanna participate

00:22:31.090 --> 00:22:34.740
in the Summer Science Research
Program, you can do so.

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:36.480
You don't need a nomination for that,

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:38.206
you can just start an application.

00:22:38.206 --> 00:22:40.380
And I think those application,

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:43.770
the deadline for that
is the same, January 4th

00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:48.700
or December 21st, I can't
remember, I have to double check.

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:50.543
But it's either December or January.

00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:57.603
So if things are opened up,
we will be meeting in-person?

00:23:01.550 --> 00:23:06.550
Probably not, so we've gone
back and forth on this,

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:10.430
like what the pandemic may
look like in the future.

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:11.513
We're hoping that maybe we can do

00:23:11.513 --> 00:23:15.587
like a quick meet and greet
outside outdoors some way.

00:23:15.587 --> 00:23:20.030
But the chances were planning
for us to not meet in-person.

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:22.090
It's just easier for us as a team

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:24.630
to plan your projects ahead of time,

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:27.050
instead of waiting to see whether or not

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:28.985
we can bring you all on campus.

00:23:28.985 --> 00:23:33.380
We're almost 100% sure that
we still won't be allowed

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:37.760
to have visitors on campus
at that time indoors.

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:39.790
For working papers, send us an email,

00:23:39.790 --> 00:23:41.483
and we can talk more about that.

00:23:43.768 --> 00:23:47.610
So we're actually working on
project development right now.

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:50.800
So we actually have a
program of scientists

00:23:52.067 --> 00:23:54.880
that will be working on
developing the summer projects

00:23:54.880 --> 00:23:56.620
and the spring projects.

00:23:56.620 --> 00:24:01.600
And so we actually won't
have a finalized project list

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:04.050
until the spring and the summer.

00:24:04.050 --> 00:24:07.460
One thing I just wanna note
is despite of the project,

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:09.410
the process is pretty much the same.

00:24:09.410 --> 00:24:13.710
We really zone in and focus on
what science is as a process.

00:24:13.710 --> 00:24:16.270
So in terms of your inspiration

00:24:16.270 --> 00:24:18.190
for starting a project, right?

00:24:18.190 --> 00:24:22.030
Observing, exploring,
asking the questions,

00:24:22.030 --> 00:24:24.233
coming up with some of your
results in your conclusions,

00:24:24.233 --> 00:24:26.335
delivering this message.

00:24:26.335 --> 00:24:30.730
Talking about iteration
of your project, failing,

00:24:30.730 --> 00:24:32.220
how do you handle that failure?

00:24:32.220 --> 00:24:35.730
Because science is, I
wanna say 90% failure,

00:24:35.730 --> 00:24:37.610
and 10% success,

00:24:37.610 --> 00:24:39.973
but that's kind of what
makes science science.

00:24:41.890 --> 00:24:43.860
What would make your
application stand out?

00:24:43.860 --> 00:24:45.024
So we look for several things.

00:24:45.024 --> 00:24:50.024
We look for keen interest,
your passion for sciences,

00:24:51.620 --> 00:24:54.823
making sure that you can
commit to that entire time.

00:24:55.860 --> 00:24:58.790
We do not look at grades.

00:24:58.790 --> 00:25:03.170
What we do look at is, have
you improved in your grade,

00:25:03.170 --> 00:25:06.123
so maybe you have like a bad
year, your 10th grade year.

00:25:06.123 --> 00:25:09.250
But your teacher wrote a
letter of recommendation

00:25:09.250 --> 00:25:10.270
and explained like,

00:25:10.270 --> 00:25:13.090
you may have had
difficulties in the subject,

00:25:13.090 --> 00:25:17.160
you worked really hard,
they're really into it,

00:25:17.160 --> 00:25:19.020
and we think that they'll be successful

00:25:19.020 --> 00:25:20.242
in a program, that's fine.

00:25:20.242 --> 00:25:22.480
We're not looking for straight A students.

00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:24.220
I don't expect you to have a 4.0,

00:25:24.220 --> 00:25:26.140
but I do expect you to work hard

00:25:27.001 --> 00:25:30.933
to be successful in the program.

00:25:32.970 --> 00:25:35.190
So the themes of this year's research.

00:25:35.190 --> 00:25:37.667
For the spring, it will be more so

00:25:37.667 --> 00:25:41.600
of talking about the scientific process

00:25:41.600 --> 00:25:43.030
within the scientific enterprise.

00:25:43.030 --> 00:25:45.280
So the project's would
look pretty much the same

00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:46.760
for everyone in the spring.

00:25:46.760 --> 00:25:51.030
The summer, people would be
off in their smaller projects,

00:25:51.030 --> 00:25:52.560
in their mentored group.

00:25:52.560 --> 00:25:55.180
And so what we do prior
to the summer session

00:25:55.180 --> 00:25:58.190
is once we get the idea of the
projects and what it entails,

00:25:58.190 --> 00:25:59.620
we'll send out a survey,

00:25:59.620 --> 00:26:03.150
and we'll try our best to match students

00:26:03.150 --> 00:26:08.150
